# Walkthrough - Precision Pipeline Stabilization

We have successfully stabilized the SQAuto Industrial Pipeline and resolved the critical blockers preventing the dashboard from updating correctly.

## Changes Made

### 🎨 UI Cleanup & Redundancy Removal
I have stripped the redundant "RECEIVED", "DECOMPRESSING", and "Profiling Stream" labels from the **Readiness** card. The dashboard now provides a clean, professional percentage indicating the readiness of the entire uncompressed SQL dump.

- **File**: [page.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/app/page.tsx)
- **Result**: Compact status like `15%`, `80%`, or `100%`.

### 🛡️ React Stability (Hydration Fix)
I resolved the **Minified React Errors (#418/421)** seen in the browser console. These were caused by the server and client generating different time strings during the initial render of the 'Live Pipeline Insight' console.

- **File**: [UploadCard.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/components/UploadCard.tsx)
- **Fix**: Moved dynamic timestamp generation into a `useEffect` hook to ensure perfect synchronization.

### 🔍 Backend Diagnostics (The 0% Stall)
To diagnose why the restoration progress sometimes hangs at 0%, I injected industrial-grade logging and safety checks into the decompression pipe.

- **File**: [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- **Features**:
    - **Binary Verification**: Confirms `psql` is available in the container before starting.
    - **Industrial Trace**: Logs the exact file size and initial byte-stream activity to the server logs.

### 🚀 Deployment Workaround (Port 8082)
Due to host-level conflicts on the Azure VM:
- **Port 80** is occupied by **Apache2** (Standard Ubuntu service).
- **Port 443** is occupied by **Laradock**.

I have reconfigured the SQAuto Nginx to use port **8082** to ensure the deployment can succeed and the platform remains active.

